Dreamcast Films: licences
=========================

Copyright (c) 2026 Jilted Valkyrie.

These works are free and are never to be sold. Two licences cover what is in this repository:

1. THE CODE: the PolyForm Noncommercial License 1.0.0 (LICENSES/PolyForm-Noncommercial-1.0.0.txt).
   That is every program and build file: in each film's folder the C sources and headers (for the first film:
   matchlight.c, matchlight_scene.h), the tests, the Makefile, and the Python tools under tools/.
   Required Notice: Copyright (c) 2026 Jilted Valkyrie (https://x.com/jiltedvalkyrie)

2. THE FILM CONTENT: Creative Commons Attribution-NonCommercial-ShareAlike 4.0 International
   (LICENSES/CC-BY-NC-SA-4.0.txt). That is the narration text (narration.json), the credit cards' text
   (credits.json), the prose of the README and other documents, any art of the author's in the repository, and
   the film as a work: its staging, shots and timing as the tables describe them.

Not covered by either licence:

- Third-party work keeps its own licence: the libraries the films are built with (KallistiOS, SH4ZAM, SH4DER-PVR, each a
  separate checkout with its own licence), the fonts, the sounds and the music a build fetches. Each film's
  THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md and CREDITS.md list them, and its LICENSES/ folder holds their texts.
- Nothing that is not in this repository is licensed by it. A disc image of a film may carry a narrator's recording,
  title art and licensed sound effects that are not here: those stay with their owners and may not be taken out of
  an image and used elsewhere.
- The tale "The Little Match Girl" by Hans Christian Andersen is in the public domain.
- "Sega" and "Dreamcast" are trademarks of their owner; these are unofficial works and no trademark right is given.
